1
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,130
Change the singer. I'm asking you.

2
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:08,070
No, Din.

3
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:10,430
If that's your only reason, I don't see the point.

4
00:00:10,430 --> 00:00:11,400
But as for me...

5
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,100
he's someone who always brings trouble.

6
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:16,370
I know Aof wants me to break up with Rei, but I can't right now.

7
00:00:16,370 --> 00:00:18,130
He's hitting on everyone.

8
00:00:18,130 --> 00:00:21,200
Nothing against you, but what you did to my friend was fucked up.

9
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:22,530
Who? Din?

10
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:23,930
You've got beef with Din too?

11
00:00:23,930 --> 00:00:26,130
Good, all at once, asshole!

12
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:28,270
I can't sing for you this evening, Star.

13
00:00:28,270 --> 00:00:29,230
I'm sorry.

14
00:00:29,230 --> 00:00:30,200
Want to give it a shot?

15
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:31,900
I'd drop dead from the shock, bro.

16
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:35,700
If you get nervous, just tell yourself you're singing this for me alone.

17
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:37,930
Look at me, and sing it for me.

18
00:00:37,930 --> 00:00:38,900
Not here to lecture you.

19
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:39,970
I'm here to help.

20
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:41,570
I called motorbike taxis for you. I get it.

21
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:44,300
My friends and I have been through this before.

22
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:46,300
Hey, Physics, don't run from me.

23
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:48,230
I'm running out of patience with you.

24
00:00:48,230 --> 00:00:49,900
So stay away from me for a while.

25
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,200
You don't want me around, huh?

26
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,730
Take it out on me, then.

27
00:00:52,730 --> 00:00:54,170
Hey, what are you—

28
00:00:55,130 --> 00:00:57,030
I'm sorry. For almost hitting you.

29
00:00:57,030 --> 00:00:58,170
I deserved it.

30
00:00:58,170 --> 00:00:59,430
Listen to me carefully.

31
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:00,470
I like you.

32
00:01:00,470 --> 00:01:02,300
Have you ever liked me, Fuen?

33
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:03,300
Star likes you.

34
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:06,470
And I promised him I'd help him win you over.

35
00:01:06,470 --> 00:01:07,570
I promise.

36
00:01:07,570 --> 00:01:10,100
No matter what, I'll stay your friend.

37
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:14,530
Din looked really cool today.

38
00:01:46,100 --> 00:01:48,600
Din looked really cool today.

39
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,400
Physics.

40
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:33,600
Whoa, finally! It's been way too long.

41
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:34,500
When did you get back?

42
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:35,930
Landed in Thailand just last night.

43
00:02:35,930 --> 00:02:37,730
I was going to surprise you at your place.

44
00:02:37,730 --> 00:02:39,030
Wanted to see your mom and dad too.

45
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:44,100
It's all right, it's all right.

46
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:45,900
But don't rush off. Want to wait and see Chemi?

47
00:02:45,900 --> 00:02:47,800
Sure. But let's go talk outside.

48
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:49,130
Too noisy in here to shout over.

49
00:02:49,130 --> 00:02:50,030
Cool, cool.

50
00:02:50,030 --> 00:02:50,930
You go on ahead.

51
00:02:50,930 --> 00:02:52,570
Then message me, yeah?

52
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:54,130
We'll talk.

53
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:07,200
It's been so long. You were really cool back there, Din.

54
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:11,870
Really?

55
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:16,370
A lot of friends were watching, so I gave it everything.

56
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:20,730
Mm. And how's your mom?

57
00:05:21,930 --> 00:05:22,970
She's fine.

58
00:05:24,700 --> 00:05:27,100
Hey, don't look so serious.

59
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:28,930
I'm not here to get back together.

60
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:35,100
I just came to say goodbye.

61
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:41,630
I'm going abroad next week.

62
00:05:42,430 --> 00:05:44,800
It'll be a long time before I'm back.

63
00:05:45,870 --> 00:05:48,170
Or maybe I won't come back at all.

64
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:54,330
I just don't want to go yet.

65
00:05:54,330 --> 00:05:56,730
Because something still feels unfinished.

66
00:06:06,330 --> 00:06:10,130
But back there, Din, you were seriously cool. Amazing.

67
00:06:16,730 --> 00:06:18,570
I hope things go well for you, Yok.

68
00:06:18,570 --> 00:06:20,130
Safe travels.

69
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:27,170
And I'm sorry for everything.

70
00:06:27,170 --> 00:06:28,530
For not taking better care of you.

71
00:06:35,930 --> 00:06:38,170
Hey, don't be so serious.

72
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:42,230
It was my own fault back then.

73
00:06:42,230 --> 00:06:45,730
Expecting too much and being selfish with you.

74
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:51,670
I have to go now.

75
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:54,070
Can I get a hug?

76
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:02,770
I'll head off, then.

77
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:26,770
Hey, why didn't you tell me you were coming back?

78
00:08:26,770 --> 00:08:28,400
Wanted to surprise me, huh.

79
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:30,400
You said you'd come see me over the break.

80
00:08:30,400 --> 00:08:31,570
You never showed.

81
00:08:31,570 --> 00:08:33,900
So I had to come to you instead.

82
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:39,500
I did plan to, I just couldn't find the right moment.

83
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,700
What a lame excuse, man.

84
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:45,300
Oh, by the way, I've picked all my universities.

85
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:46,700
I kind of cheated on London.

86
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:50,270
Hooked on the sea. The vibe there is unreal.

87
00:08:50,270 --> 00:08:52,500
See? And back then,

88
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:54,600
you said you loved London so much.

89
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:57,230
Wanted nothing but London. And now?

90
00:08:57,230 --> 00:08:59,370
I called it. Bournemouth suits you.

91
00:08:59,370 --> 00:09:02,900
Who else goes all-in on London like you, huh?

92
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:10,200
You never know.

93
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,630
How would you know?

94
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:14,900
Maybe one day I'll change my mind.

95
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:17,300
This changing-your-mind thing...

96
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:19,170
It wouldn't be about...

97
00:09:22,870 --> 00:09:24,370
Now you've got me curious.

98
00:09:24,370 --> 00:09:26,130
What would make you change your mind?

99
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:33,470
Let's just say there's something.

100
00:09:36,270 --> 00:09:37,770
You could probably guess.

101
00:09:48,030 --> 00:09:50,800
I only just found out this was Star's idea.

102
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:54,400
Back in our year, I thought Din went big. Right, Din?

103
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:59,930
But Star's is even bigger. Incredible.

104
00:10:01,170 --> 00:10:04,400
So you and Din did all this in your year too?

105
00:10:05,700 --> 00:10:09,530
Back then we ran a booth selling stuff as well.

106
00:10:09,530 --> 00:10:10,970
It nearly killed us.

107
00:10:10,970 --> 00:10:13,630
Seriously. All of us in M.6

108
00:10:13,630 --> 00:10:16,500
had to scoop ice until our hands went numb.

109
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:18,200
And Physics and Tang

110
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:21,230
had to wear mascot suits waving customers in like lucky cats.

111
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:25,430
And this year, big thanks to FUN VIBE.

112
00:10:25,430 --> 00:10:27,300
All of you. You were great.

113
00:10:31,230 --> 00:10:34,630
So that's why you've been putting this much pressure on me?

114
00:10:34,630 --> 00:10:36,600
Because you did the same in your year.

115
00:10:38,670 --> 00:10:42,730
Everyone, listen up.

116
00:10:45,830 --> 00:10:48,600
Total donations, transfers and cash,

117
00:10:48,600 --> 00:10:51,570
23,500 baht!

118
00:10:53,530 --> 00:10:56,100
Amazing!

119
00:11:06,670 --> 00:11:10,730
Okay, so once everyone's helped me pack up,

120
00:11:11,970 --> 00:11:15,030
come have moo kratha at my place. My treat.

121
00:11:22,730 --> 00:11:25,000
Hey, Din, where'd you disappear to all this time?

122
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:26,730
I thought you'd gone home ages ago.

123
00:11:26,730 --> 00:11:28,270
I'm not you, mate.

124
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:32,130
If you're free, Din, you should come along.

125
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:34,970
Go on, we're all going anyway.

126
00:11:35,630 --> 00:11:38,470
Well, isn't that sweet.

127
00:11:52,530 --> 00:11:54,330
Ow.

128
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:10,770
Our grill isn't like yours.

129
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:13,200
Top, it's all right.

130
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:14,600
We can grill it ourselves.

131
00:12:16,730 --> 00:12:18,400
Dig in, everyone.

132
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:20,930
Come on, hurry.

133
00:12:33,970 --> 00:12:36,630
So, camp all planned, Star?

134
00:12:37,170 --> 00:12:40,100
Not yet, but almost there.

135
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:43,700
Just the camp activities left. I'm afraid no one will enjoy them.

136
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:45,370
Honestly, whether it's fun or not,

137
00:12:45,370 --> 00:12:47,600
I think it depends more on what kind of game it is.

138
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:51,270
If it's competitive, teamwork-based, or fighting over prizes,

139
00:12:51,270 --> 00:12:52,470
you'll be fine either way.

140
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:54,530
That's true.

141
00:12:55,100 --> 00:12:57,630
Then once I'm done, I'll bring it over for you to look at.

142
00:12:57,630 --> 00:12:58,970
Mm, of course.

143
00:12:59,700 --> 00:13:03,100
I had no idea Din and Star were close.

144
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:09,170
We're not. Honestly, before this, Din and I barely talked.

145
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:12,200
We only started talking because of the work.

146
00:13:13,670 --> 00:13:15,030
Just like he said.

147
00:13:15,030 --> 00:13:18,170
But if you're free and want something to do, Fuen, come help out.

148
00:13:22,430 --> 00:13:24,430
There are plenty more projects this year.

149
00:13:24,430 --> 00:13:26,070
You'd have fun, Fuen.

150
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:31,630
Or if you're ever short-handed, just call me in.

151
00:13:31,630 --> 00:13:32,930
I'll come help.

152
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:39,100
Hey, Din, I want your advice about university.

153
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:41,570
Sure. Got any faculties in mind yet?

154
00:13:42,630 --> 00:13:47,700
Nope. No idea what to study. I ask Physics and he always changes the subject.

155
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:56,770
Just take it easy. There's still time, right?

156
00:13:58,700 --> 00:14:01,300
Then how about the arts faculties?

157
00:14:01,300 --> 00:14:03,770
Communication arts, architecture, something like that.

158
00:14:03,770 --> 00:14:06,400
If it's architecture, your dad could help, Fuen.

159
00:14:07,530 --> 00:14:09,730
Mm, true.

160
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:13,870
Problem is, he never lets up on work.

161
00:14:13,870 --> 00:14:18,600
Home once or twice a month. Now he's off supervising a site again.

162
00:14:20,230 --> 00:14:22,600
Then try... / Hey, Fuen.

163
00:14:23,670 --> 00:14:28,970
I reckon you need some salad in your life, man.

164
00:14:28,970 --> 00:14:30,530
Your health's going to suffer.

165
00:14:30,530 --> 00:14:32,930
What if you end up short on vita— vitamins?

166
00:14:36,800 --> 00:14:38,600
Oh, thank you.

167
00:14:43,400 --> 00:14:45,600
It dropped.

168
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:47,800
Ugh, Chok.

169
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:49,900
Chok, is it cooked yet?

170
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:26,670
You don't like shrimp?

171
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:30,200
I do.

172
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:31,870
So why only pork?

173
00:15:33,630 --> 00:15:35,470
I can't peel shrimp.

174
00:15:37,130 --> 00:15:38,500
Just say so next time.

175
00:15:47,130 --> 00:15:48,600
I'll peel them for you.

176
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:52,200
Thank you, Din.

177
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:10,200
Ooh, shrimp.

178
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:32,600
What happened to you, Aof? You're hurt.

179
00:16:36,430 --> 00:16:38,330
I ran into a bit of trouble.

180
00:16:38,330 --> 00:16:40,700
Why haven't you cleaned it?

181
00:16:40,700 --> 00:16:42,970
At least put some ointment on it.

182
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:45,670
I'm tough.

183
00:16:53,670 --> 00:16:55,530
Aof, lean your head down.

184
00:17:12,569 --> 00:17:16,470
Could you move back a little?

185
00:17:28,069 --> 00:17:30,870
I'll back up. This should make it easier.

186
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:39,570
Shift back a little.

187
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:49,770
Sorry.

188
00:17:55,070 --> 00:17:56,400
All done.

189
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:02,370
Sorry about that.

190
00:18:02,370 --> 00:18:04,930
Thank you so much for today, Aof.

191
00:18:04,930 --> 00:18:08,170
Without you, I'd never have managed.

192
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:10,630
What are you thanking me for?

193
00:18:10,630 --> 00:18:12,730
I barely did anything today.

194
00:18:26,270 --> 00:18:29,270
Either way, thank you so much.

195
00:18:35,300 --> 00:18:37,000
Thanks.

196
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:09,070
Bro! You up yet? Leave late and you'll hit traffic.

197
00:19:09,070 --> 00:19:10,600
See you downstairs, bro.

198
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:12,770
I'll be waiting downstairs. Hurry up.

199
00:19:16,130 --> 00:19:20,500
What's the rush? The bus doesn't leave till 7:50.

200
00:19:22,230 --> 00:19:24,270
Shit, it's 7:40.

201
00:19:38,930 --> 00:19:42,100
Dad, I'm heading off now.

202
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:44,570
Oh, leaving already?

203
00:19:44,570 --> 00:19:47,230
So is the place you're staying safe?

204
00:19:47,230 --> 00:19:49,970
Should I send Samai along to look after you?

205
00:19:49,970 --> 00:19:51,300
It's fine, Dad.

206
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:53,800
What about money, have you got enough? Here.

207
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:57,070
I'm fine. I still have what you gave me last time.

208
00:19:57,070 --> 00:19:59,700
And what if there's an emergency?

209
00:19:59,700 --> 00:20:01,470
Then take my card.

210
00:20:03,870 --> 00:20:07,200
It's fine, Dad. There aren't any ATMs out there.

211
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:08,900
Then take my gold.

212
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:11,470
Dad, don't overdo it.

213
00:20:12,630 --> 00:20:14,300
I'm joking.

214
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:16,330
I'm only going to camp, Dad.

215
00:20:16,330 --> 00:20:19,100
I'll be back safe and sound, I promise.

216
00:20:19,470 --> 00:20:21,170
Then give me a hug.

217
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:25,100
Safe travels, son.

218
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:27,700
Yes, Dad. / I worry about you.

219
00:20:29,670 --> 00:20:31,300
Good luck. / Thanks.

220
00:20:31,300 --> 00:20:33,000
See you.

221
00:20:34,300 --> 00:20:36,700
Samai, take good care of him. / Yes, sir.

222
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:54,900
Here I come.

223
00:20:56,270 --> 00:20:57,800
Fuen. / Am I on time?

224
00:20:57,800 --> 00:21:00,800
Fuen, M.6. / You made it. Put your bag on the bus.

225
00:21:03,330 --> 00:21:06,100
Whoa, you're early.

226
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:07,200
Of course I am.

227
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:08,670
Thought I'd see you chasing the bus.

228
00:21:08,670 --> 00:21:11,330
Whoa, that was back in primary school.

229
00:21:11,330 --> 00:21:14,170
I couldn't chase a bus now if I tried.

230
00:21:14,170 --> 00:21:17,500
Hey, since we're on primary school, here.

231
00:21:19,330 --> 00:21:20,900
Take this onto the bus for me.

232
00:21:20,900 --> 00:21:22,600
Sure. / Come gossip then.

233
00:21:22,600 --> 00:21:23,470
Okay, okay.

234
00:21:26,470 --> 00:21:30,400
Then Physics can sit somewhere else. Bye, see you.

235
00:21:34,130 --> 00:21:37,400
Give the name cards to Physics and Chemi.

236
00:21:38,130 --> 00:21:40,000
Damn, you're really going for it.

237
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:41,730
You're serious this time?

238
00:21:44,270 --> 00:21:46,100
I think it'll be tough.

239
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:49,570
Physics won't let you cut in that easily.

240
00:21:53,700 --> 00:21:58,470
I'll try. If it doesn't work out, fine. At least I gave it everything.

241
00:22:01,970 --> 00:22:04,770
I don't want to sit around regretting it later.

242
00:22:09,570 --> 00:22:11,630
Um, Star.

243
00:22:11,630 --> 00:22:14,830
If I get on first, can I save a seat?

244
00:22:14,830 --> 00:22:15,770
Sure.

245
00:22:15,770 --> 00:22:18,200
Whoever gets on first picks first.

246
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:21,030
But you have to pick within your year's zone.

247
00:22:27,530 --> 00:22:29,600
Thank you. / Sure.

248
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:39,570
Everything's here.

249
00:22:39,570 --> 00:22:41,270
Whoa, it really is.

250
00:22:41,630 --> 00:22:42,500
All set.

251
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:45,130
Okay. Good luck.

252
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:45,500
Ugh, the traffic was insane today.

253
00:23:46,500 --> 00:23:48,030
And I even left early.

254
00:23:48,030 --> 00:23:49,700
Early by your standards is what time?

255
00:23:49,700 --> 00:23:51,770
I woke up and called you and you were still asleep.

256
00:23:52,370 --> 00:23:54,030
Don't count from when I left.

257
00:23:54,030 --> 00:23:56,830
I'm here now, aren't I? I made it. Happy ending.

258
00:23:56,830 --> 00:23:59,800
Just let him brag a bit, or else

259
00:24:00,300 --> 00:24:02,670
you'll see him climbing in through the bus window.

260
00:24:02,670 --> 00:24:04,300
Physics, I'm your friend, remember?

261
00:24:04,300 --> 00:24:05,130
Sure thing, friend.

262
00:24:05,870 --> 00:24:07,300
And what's with Fuen?

263
00:24:07,930 --> 00:24:09,330
Got here and went straight to sleep.

264
00:24:10,100 --> 00:24:11,670
Just let this one sleep.

265
00:24:11,670 --> 00:24:14,700
He was probably up all night with his new game.

266
00:24:14,700 --> 00:24:15,770
Played it till morning.

267
00:24:15,770 --> 00:24:17,130
Then I'm getting some sleep too.

268
00:24:21,130 --> 00:24:22,830
Tang! You're heavy!

269
00:24:22,830 --> 00:24:24,230
Keep it down. / I'm heavy.

270
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:27,770
Fine, you win.

271
00:25:03,500 --> 00:25:05,570
Looks like I'll have to sit with you.

272
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:19,300
Star...

273
00:25:23,070 --> 00:25:27,830
Um, I can go find a seat at the back.

274
00:25:27,830 --> 00:25:31,230
Hi, Din... make yourself comfortable.

275
00:25:40,500 --> 00:25:44,400
Mind if I make myself comfortable for the ride?

276
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:45,500
Oh, sure, go ahead.

277
00:25:45,500 --> 00:25:46,830
Excuse me.

278
00:25:49,730 --> 00:25:51,670
Just kidding.

279
00:25:59,130 --> 00:26:00,430
I know.

280
00:26:02,530 --> 00:26:03,930
You sure?

281
00:26:05,370 --> 00:26:08,070
It's obvious you like...

282
00:26:08,770 --> 00:26:10,030
Tonnam.

283
00:27:11,370 --> 00:27:12,270
Fuen.

284
00:27:12,600 --> 00:27:14,070
Watch where you're walking.

285
00:27:14,070 --> 00:27:15,100
Keep your eyes open, too.

286
00:27:15,100 --> 00:27:17,070
What if you trip and land on your face?

287
00:27:17,070 --> 00:27:18,230
I am watching.

288
00:27:19,530 --> 00:27:20,700
Whoa!

289
00:27:24,630 --> 00:27:25,970
So beautiful.

290
00:27:27,430 --> 00:27:29,470
Aof, hand me your bag.

291
00:27:36,070 --> 00:27:38,070
Here, my bag. I'll carry it myself.

292
00:27:38,070 --> 00:27:39,370
Just walk. I'll carry it.

293
00:27:39,370 --> 00:27:41,300
How long are you two going to fight over that bag?

294
00:27:41,300 --> 00:27:45,100
Here, Physics, my bag. You carry it.

295
00:27:50,700 --> 00:27:53,430
If you can't carry your own bag,

296
00:27:53,430 --> 00:27:55,930
then just chuck it in the water.

297
00:27:55,930 --> 00:27:57,400
Physics.

298
00:27:59,230 --> 00:28:02,600
I give up. I've got two pairs of underwear in there.

299
00:28:04,030 --> 00:28:05,800
See what he's really like now?

300
00:28:07,370 --> 00:28:09,130
So when are you going to stop?

301
00:28:09,130 --> 00:28:10,370
Stop what?

302
00:28:10,370 --> 00:28:12,130
Stop messing with my brother.

303
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:14,270
You think I don't know?

304
00:28:15,670 --> 00:28:17,330
Chemi. / Yes?

305
00:28:17,330 --> 00:28:18,900
Come walk with your big brother.

306
00:28:20,300 --> 00:28:21,830
Come walk with me instead.

307
00:28:21,830 --> 00:28:23,000
Come on, let's go.

308
00:28:30,030 --> 00:28:33,230
Honestly, you should stop winding Physics up.

309
00:28:33,800 --> 00:28:36,000
Your score with him is already deep in the negatives.

310
00:28:36,630 --> 00:28:40,300
Easy for you to say. You know how hard it is.

311
00:28:42,330 --> 00:28:46,030
I still can't work out how I'm supposed to ask him.

312
00:28:47,130 --> 00:28:48,470
Physics.

313
00:28:50,770 --> 00:28:52,600
Aof surrenders, completely.

314
00:28:53,630 --> 00:28:55,930
Aof won't hurt anyone,

315
00:28:55,930 --> 00:28:58,370
and no one will get hurt because of Aof ever again.

316
00:28:58,370 --> 00:29:01,630
So give in to Aof, please? Please, please, please.

317
00:29:01,630 --> 00:29:02,800
As if he'd ever give in to you.

318
00:29:02,800 --> 00:29:04,400
See how tough it is now?

319
00:29:04,400 --> 00:29:05,630
Go ask him yourself.

320
00:29:19,100 --> 00:29:22,230
All right, everyone, listen up. Now that we're here at camp,

321
00:29:22,230 --> 00:29:26,170
welcome, everyone, to the 11th Science Smart Camp,

322
00:29:26,170 --> 00:29:27,870
officially. Let's have a hand.

323
00:29:30,170 --> 00:29:33,400
This year it's run by our M.5 juniors.

324
00:29:33,400 --> 00:29:35,100
So let's give them a hand.

325
00:29:38,100 --> 00:29:40,470
There are a lot of activities this year, so

326
00:29:40,470 --> 00:29:44,300
I want everyone to get along and stick together.

327
00:29:44,300 --> 00:29:46,630
Whatever we're doing, cooperate with the juniors.

328
00:29:46,630 --> 00:29:50,570
And get closer to each other through this camp.

329
00:29:50,570 --> 00:29:51,600
All right?

330
00:29:51,600 --> 00:29:54,100
So let's have Satayu kick things off. Go ahead.

331
00:30:03,930 --> 00:30:08,000
Then let's start with the first activity.

332
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:11,100
It's an activity to help everyone get to know each other better.

333
00:30:18,970 --> 00:30:26,630
So I'd like everyone to split into four groups,

334
00:30:26,630 --> 00:30:33,730
six per group, and each group will have...

335
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:44,700
Everyone.

336
00:30:46,330 --> 00:30:48,430
Let's all listen to Star.

337
00:30:49,430 --> 00:30:51,600
For this Science Smart camp,

338
00:30:51,600 --> 00:30:54,430
Star and the juniors over here are in charge.

339
00:30:54,430 --> 00:30:55,930
They're the main staff.

340
00:30:55,930 --> 00:30:57,800
And the student council

341
00:30:57,800 --> 00:31:00,070
will be helping look after everything.

342
00:31:00,800 --> 00:31:02,570
Since we've come this far together,

343
00:31:03,030 --> 00:31:06,300
let's make this camp a memory we all keep.

344
00:31:08,630 --> 00:31:10,170
Our singer!

345
00:31:12,530 --> 00:31:14,230
Din is so damn cool.

346
00:31:16,930 --> 00:31:19,130
So what's next, Star?

347
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:21,900
Okay, let's start with the first activity.

348
00:31:21,900 --> 00:31:24,270
It's an activity to help us get to know each other faster.

349
00:31:24,270 --> 00:31:26,470
We'll split into four groups,

350
00:31:26,470 --> 00:31:29,130
with mixed year levels in each group.

351
00:31:29,830 --> 00:31:32,930
Our first activity is called

352
00:31:32,930 --> 00:31:35,900
How Much Do We Love Each Other.

353
00:31:44,270 --> 00:31:45,970
You've all seen the colored paper.

354
00:31:45,970 --> 00:31:49,030
This game is very simple. Every team

355
00:31:49,030 --> 00:31:50,930
has to get every member standing on the paper.

356
00:31:50,930 --> 00:31:53,100
But there's one condition: the paper must not tear.

357
00:31:53,100 --> 00:31:55,430
If it tears, the whole team loses.

358
00:31:55,430 --> 00:31:58,470
And every single member has to be standing on it.

359
00:31:58,470 --> 00:32:00,400
Anyone who can't stand on it with their team

360
00:32:00,400 --> 00:32:02,770
is out immediately as an individual.

361
00:32:02,770 --> 00:32:04,730
If everyone's ready, let's begin.

362
00:32:30,900 --> 00:32:32,770
Who's hurting the staff?

363
00:32:56,700 --> 00:33:00,530
Aof, this paper is tiny.

364
00:33:00,970 --> 00:33:02,900
How are we all supposed to stand on it?

365
00:33:09,730 --> 00:33:11,700
Let me think for a second.

366
00:33:15,400 --> 00:33:17,770
Maybe we should just give up?

367
00:33:18,900 --> 00:33:21,870
I think we can do it. Trust me.

368
00:33:24,530 --> 00:33:28,270
Um, will you be all right, Din, if I have to stand on your feet?

369
00:33:29,400 --> 00:33:30,670
Let's give it a try.

370
00:33:32,330 --> 00:33:33,600
Giving up? / Whoa.

371
00:33:33,600 --> 00:33:35,470
There's not enough room.

372
00:33:36,300 --> 00:33:38,670
Whoa. I'll just carry you.

373
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:43,800
If you did, my feet would hang over the edge.

374
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:45,300
I'm not stupid, you know.

375
00:33:46,430 --> 00:33:47,670
Trust me.

376
00:33:47,670 --> 00:33:49,800
You can start the game.

377
00:34:04,230 --> 00:34:07,300
I told you. And weren't you going to carry me?

378
00:34:07,300 --> 00:34:08,270
Sorry.

379
00:34:08,630 --> 00:34:09,600
Come here.

380
00:34:13,730 --> 00:34:15,730
Wait, wait, wait.

381
00:34:16,500 --> 00:34:17,969
Chemi, you get on first.

382
00:34:29,230 --> 00:34:30,199
Wait, wait.

383
00:34:34,070 --> 00:34:36,100
You okay? / That hurt.

384
00:34:36,100 --> 00:34:38,330
Sorry, sorry. I'm sorry.

385
00:34:44,600 --> 00:34:46,030
I'm really sorry.

386
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:49,370
I'm okay.

387
00:35:04,630 --> 00:35:09,130
Hey, hey, hey.

388
00:35:09,130 --> 00:35:10,570
That's cool, man.

389
00:35:12,100 --> 00:35:13,900
And we have our winning team.

390
00:35:13,900 --> 00:35:16,200
It's Tang and Time.

391
00:35:28,370 --> 00:35:30,270
Thirsty, man? / I'm thirsty.

392
00:35:30,270 --> 00:35:31,900
Thirsty? / Tang.

393
00:35:31,900 --> 00:35:33,270
If you're thirsty, drink up.

394
00:35:33,270 --> 00:35:35,030
Then hand it over so I can drink.

395
00:35:38,970 --> 00:35:40,470
Chemi. / Huh?

396
00:35:40,470 --> 00:35:42,530
So did you ask Aof or not?

397
00:35:43,800 --> 00:35:44,870
Not yet.

398
00:35:47,500 --> 00:35:51,830
I try to ask, and Aof cuts in.

399
00:35:51,830 --> 00:35:54,870
There's always something getting in the way.

400
00:35:55,730 --> 00:35:59,700
I want to know too, what he actually wants.

401
00:36:01,830 --> 00:36:04,400
Aren't you scared, though?

402
00:36:04,400 --> 00:36:06,870
That the answer won't be what you're hoping for?

403
00:36:07,530 --> 00:36:10,130
Right. I've wondered about that too.

404
00:36:10,130 --> 00:36:12,500
If he really has liked you since back then,

405
00:36:12,500 --> 00:36:14,130
while he was waiting for you to grow up,

406
00:36:14,130 --> 00:36:16,230
how did he hold back and do nothing all that time?

407
00:36:16,230 --> 00:36:17,500
Yeah, exactly.

408
00:36:25,530 --> 00:36:31,430
This friend of mine is cute, kind, easy to get along with.

409
00:36:31,430 --> 00:36:33,600
Just a bit of a nutcase.

410
00:36:36,230 --> 00:36:38,030
Was that a compliment?

411
00:36:38,030 --> 00:36:40,230
Of course it was. Who wouldn't compliment you?

412
00:36:42,330 --> 00:36:43,900
But surely he's been dropping hints,

413
00:36:43,900 --> 00:36:46,800
or sending you some kind of special signal?

414
00:36:46,800 --> 00:36:47,700
Yeah.

415
00:37:02,530 --> 00:37:05,870
From back then until just before I got to upper secondary,

416
00:37:06,430 --> 00:37:08,000
there was nothing special.

417
00:37:10,130 --> 00:37:15,030
He came and went. Sometimes he looked after me, sometimes he didn't.

418
00:37:15,030 --> 00:37:16,730
Same as my brother does.

419
00:37:18,570 --> 00:37:24,230
But the big thing is, he avoided ever being alone with me.

420
00:37:27,900 --> 00:37:33,300
And now, out of nowhere, he's being good to me.

421
00:37:45,230 --> 00:37:46,970
That's exactly why I'm so confused.

422
00:37:46,970 --> 00:37:50,530
So what he's doing now is something special, then.

423
00:37:51,030 --> 00:37:53,530
You're just afraid he's only playing with you.

424
00:37:54,500 --> 00:37:56,570
If I'm not imagining it.

425
00:37:56,570 --> 00:38:01,130
If you don't want it hanging over you, go talk to him tonight.

426
00:38:01,870 --> 00:38:03,030
Is that really a good idea?

427
00:38:03,030 --> 00:38:04,930
Why wouldn't it be?

428
00:38:04,930 --> 00:38:09,670
If you like someone and you hesitate, it means you're not serious.

429
00:38:13,270 --> 00:38:15,930
Talking to you guys is painful.

430
00:38:17,630 --> 00:38:19,770
I should've just talked to Chat instead.

431
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:24,200
I'm out. / How was what I said painful?

432
00:38:24,200 --> 00:38:26,270
Or does the pain actually hurt?

433
00:38:27,170 --> 00:38:29,570
But the pain really does hurt.

434
00:38:51,530 --> 00:38:56,770
All right, everyone, we're starting activity two. Ready?

435
00:38:56,770 --> 00:38:59,000
If you're ready, let's go over the rules first.

436
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:00,300
Go ahead, Star.

437
00:39:00,300 --> 00:39:03,000
Our second game is a pass-the-object game.

438
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:05,430
You're not allowed to use your hands to pass it.

439
00:39:05,430 --> 00:39:08,700
We'll draw lots to see which body part you use.

440
00:39:09,730 --> 00:39:11,330
Okay, so as I said,

441
00:39:11,330 --> 00:39:14,100
you use the body part you draw to pass the object down the line.

442
00:39:14,100 --> 00:39:17,530
The key rule is, you can't switch body parts.

443
00:39:17,970 --> 00:39:19,870
And the first team to play

444
00:39:19,870 --> 00:39:21,770
is the M.6 team.

445
00:39:21,770 --> 00:39:23,400
Let's give them a hand.

446
00:39:25,370 --> 00:39:28,930
And finally, we have a very special surprise for everyone.

447
00:39:28,930 --> 00:39:32,030
Jamesphorn will be joining this activity with us.

448
00:39:35,400 --> 00:39:37,370
Smile, smile. Big smile.

449
00:39:37,370 --> 00:39:39,030
Come on, up you get.

450
00:39:39,030 --> 00:39:40,230
Come on, come on.

451
00:39:40,230 --> 00:39:41,500
Let's start the game.

452
00:39:44,430 --> 00:39:46,730
Starting with Aof first.

453
00:39:49,070 --> 00:39:50,300
Big toe.

454
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:02,170
Whoa, what is it? / Come on, tell him.

455
00:40:02,170 --> 00:40:03,670
Mouth.

456
00:40:09,570 --> 00:40:11,230
Shoulder.

457
00:40:15,070 --> 00:40:16,800
Between the legs.

458
00:40:21,730 --> 00:40:23,170
Mouth.

459
00:40:25,870 --> 00:40:27,230
Chin.

460
00:40:29,800 --> 00:40:30,870
Hip.

461
00:40:32,900 --> 00:40:34,870
Ow, Thanop, come on.

462
00:40:36,470 --> 00:40:38,070
Back of the knee.

463
00:40:42,200 --> 00:40:44,500
Bam! Head.

464
00:41:27,230 --> 00:41:30,230
Okay, everyone, that's two games down.

465
00:41:30,230 --> 00:41:31,400
Now for the last game.

466
00:41:31,400 --> 00:41:32,670
How's everyone doing?

467
00:41:34,200 --> 00:41:35,900
Okay, our final game

468
00:41:35,900 --> 00:41:37,300
is hide-and-seek.

469
00:41:37,300 --> 00:41:39,330
Not the ordinary hide-and-seek you've played before.

470
00:41:39,330 --> 00:41:41,730
You have to carry one of these items with you.

471
00:41:41,730 --> 00:41:44,030
You can hide anywhere inside the resort,

472
00:41:44,030 --> 00:41:45,600
but no going into the woods.

473
00:41:45,600 --> 00:41:47,770
The hiding team takes an item from here,

474
00:41:47,770 --> 00:41:50,370
and the seeking team takes a card from here.

475
00:41:50,370 --> 00:41:53,930
The seekers have to find the person matching the item on their card.

476
00:41:53,930 --> 00:41:56,300
You have two hours to find them.

477
00:41:56,300 --> 00:41:58,500
If you don't find everyone, or time runs out,

478
00:41:58,500 --> 00:42:00,770
that team loses.

479
00:42:00,770 --> 00:42:03,430
So seekers, come and take your cards,

480
00:42:03,430 --> 00:42:05,800
and hiders, come and take your items here.

481
00:42:05,800 --> 00:42:08,500
Okay, hiders, off you go.

482
00:42:20,800 --> 00:42:21,670
That blends in?

483
00:42:21,670 --> 00:42:22,430
It blends.

484
00:42:26,270 --> 00:42:30,000
I bet someone's hiding behind that tent.

485
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:31,600
I think so too.

486
00:42:46,030 --> 00:42:47,900
I told you.

487
00:42:49,130 --> 00:42:50,600
Whoa, Fuen.

488
00:42:51,900 --> 00:42:53,870
We're the first two caught?

489
00:42:53,870 --> 00:42:55,930
Yep, you two are the first.

490
00:42:57,970 --> 00:42:59,230
Let's see what you've got.

491
00:43:01,700 --> 00:43:03,270
Where's the test tube?

492
00:43:13,670 --> 00:43:16,470
Are you sure this spot works?

493
00:43:16,470 --> 00:43:18,970
Of course. The most dangerous place

494
00:43:18,970 --> 00:43:20,670
is the safest damn place there is.

495
00:43:20,670 --> 00:43:22,130
If we can't find anywhere to hide,

496
00:43:22,130 --> 00:43:23,800
we just hide right here.

497
00:43:23,800 --> 00:43:25,970
You don't think people will come for water?

498
00:43:27,170 --> 00:43:29,130
Oh yeah. Didn't think of that.

499
00:43:29,130 --> 00:43:31,430
Asshole, move. What the hell are you waiting for?

500
00:43:38,030 --> 00:43:39,870
Stop right there.

501
00:43:42,430 --> 00:43:44,300
Oh, damn.

502
00:43:46,270 --> 00:43:48,470
All three of you. / Peekaboo.

503
00:43:49,500 --> 00:43:50,330
Hello there.

504
00:43:53,300 --> 00:43:55,630
That's not your card, you know.

505
00:43:58,430 --> 00:43:59,930
What's going on?

506
00:43:59,930 --> 00:44:01,930
And you, that's confiscated.

507
00:44:01,930 --> 00:44:03,370
Sure thing.

508
00:44:03,730 --> 00:44:05,230
That one too.

509
00:44:20,600 --> 00:44:22,600
No one would be hiding here, right?

510
00:44:22,600 --> 00:44:24,800
Nope. / Good, what a relief.

511
00:44:26,000 --> 00:44:27,630
Hey! Is this funny to you?

512
00:44:29,900 --> 00:44:32,730
Get up. I've caught you.

513
00:44:37,330 --> 00:44:38,670
Potassium.

514
00:44:41,030 --> 00:44:44,170
I've got a balloon. Not what you're looking for.

515
00:44:44,170 --> 00:44:46,100
Then I'll keep hiding.

516
00:44:51,830 --> 00:44:53,600
Where the hell did you all hide?

517
00:44:53,600 --> 00:44:55,570
No hiding for me. I'm the seeker.

518
00:44:55,570 --> 00:44:56,500
Hey.

519
00:44:58,500 --> 00:45:00,370
Where did everyone disappear to?

520
00:45:04,670 --> 00:45:06,100
Thanop! Tonnam!

521
00:45:06,570 --> 00:45:08,130
What have you got in your hands?

522
00:45:10,400 --> 00:45:11,570
Busted.

523
00:45:11,570 --> 00:45:12,770
I'm not giving it to you.

524
00:45:12,770 --> 00:45:13,800
You're going to get it.

525
00:45:13,800 --> 00:45:15,900
Not giving it, not giving it.

526
00:45:23,100 --> 00:45:26,030
Um, who haven't we found yet?

527
00:45:26,030 --> 00:45:28,630
I think it's just Physics and Tang left.

528
00:45:28,630 --> 00:45:30,500
Or did they run off home?

529
00:45:30,500 --> 00:45:32,200
We can't find them anywhere.

530
00:45:33,770 --> 00:45:36,330
How many minutes do we have left?

531
00:45:36,330 --> 00:45:38,400
About 20 minutes.

532
00:45:38,970 --> 00:45:40,470
Then let's split up.

533
00:45:41,030 --> 00:45:42,870
Time, you come with me.

534
00:45:42,870 --> 00:45:44,300
Then Star and Jay, come with me.

535
00:45:44,300 --> 00:45:45,230
Okay. / Got it.

536
00:45:45,230 --> 00:45:46,330
Go, go. Time, come on.

537
00:45:47,830 --> 00:45:48,930
Physics.

538
00:46:02,130 --> 00:46:03,570
A perfect carbon copy.

539
00:46:03,570 --> 00:46:04,870
Now how do we get down?

540
00:46:05,270 --> 00:46:06,070
Yeah, right?

541
00:46:21,300 --> 00:46:23,470
Aren't we taking this a bit too seriously?

542
00:46:24,670 --> 00:46:26,470
Then why didn't you stop me?

543
00:46:26,470 --> 00:46:28,200
And you still followed me.

544
00:46:28,430 --> 00:46:29,670
You and me, seriously.

545
00:46:31,930 --> 00:46:33,800
What now? / What?

546
00:46:33,800 --> 00:46:35,070
Just walk out and get caught?

547
00:46:35,070 --> 00:46:36,330
My whole body's killing me.

548
00:46:38,930 --> 00:46:40,330
I'm telling you right now,

549
00:46:41,300 --> 00:46:43,070
even if someone falls in the water right here,

550
00:46:43,070 --> 00:46:45,230
I'm not coming out.

551
00:46:53,630 --> 00:46:55,930
Time, you take the left. I'll take the right.

552
00:46:55,930 --> 00:46:57,130
Okay.

553
00:46:57,130 --> 00:46:58,800
Someone's definitely hiding around here.

554
00:47:16,130 --> 00:47:17,500
Hey, where are you going?

555
00:47:18,330 --> 00:47:19,270
Hey, Fuen!

556
00:47:42,830 --> 00:47:44,830
Why can't you be more careful?

557
00:47:48,700 --> 00:47:50,470
What if I hadn't got to you in time?

558
00:47:55,270 --> 00:47:59,570
Thanks for saving me, but... I've caught you.

559
00:48:05,670 --> 00:48:06,900
Always messing around.

560
00:48:06,900 --> 00:48:07,770
Damn it.

561
00:48:14,100 --> 00:48:15,400
Bang.

562
00:48:19,800 --> 00:48:21,370
I've found you.

563
00:48:29,970 --> 00:48:32,270
Um, aren't you stiff?

564
00:48:46,630 --> 00:48:48,600
Made me sit here for so long.

565
00:48:53,570 --> 00:48:55,470
Um, if you don't mind,

566
00:48:56,130 --> 00:48:57,870
may I?

567
00:49:36,870 --> 00:49:38,700
Hey, thanks, Din.

568
00:49:39,370 --> 00:49:41,200
You too. Thanks.

569
00:49:50,130 --> 00:49:52,070
How did they end up here?

570
00:50:11,700 --> 00:50:13,430
If it's bothering you,

571
00:50:13,430 --> 00:50:15,130
shouldn't you make a decision?

572
00:50:15,130 --> 00:50:16,470
Decide what?

573
00:50:17,770 --> 00:50:19,600
About those two both chasing after you.

574
00:50:19,930 --> 00:50:20,700
Huh!

575
00:50:24,100 --> 00:50:27,000
I mean, Physics I sort of knew about.

576
00:50:27,000 --> 00:50:28,500
But Din too?

577
00:50:30,830 --> 00:50:32,330
Whoa.

578
00:50:34,230 --> 00:50:35,970
What am I supposed to do?

579
00:50:36,300 --> 00:50:38,130
I'm scared of losing my friends.

580
00:50:40,830 --> 00:50:42,330
What are you so scared of?

581
00:50:42,670 --> 00:50:46,200
When those two went after you, neither of them worried about losing you.

582
00:50:47,230 --> 00:50:49,970
I think they've already prepared themselves for it.

583
00:50:51,030 --> 00:50:53,330
If you don't believe me, why not talk to them straight?

584
00:50:55,470 --> 00:50:57,730
You don't have to be so nice about it.

585
00:50:57,730 --> 00:50:59,530
Just do what your heart tells you.

586
00:51:01,700 --> 00:51:06,400
With Physics, I know he can still be my friend.

587
00:51:07,430 --> 00:51:09,930
But Din? I have no idea.

588
00:51:12,430 --> 00:51:14,330
If you don't know, just ask him.

589
00:51:15,300 --> 00:51:16,900
Trust me.

590
00:51:16,900 --> 00:51:18,800
Neither of them is going to walk away from you.

591
00:51:20,470 --> 00:51:22,500
But I would.

592
00:51:24,530 --> 00:51:27,230
Tang, you're still messing around.

593
00:51:27,230 --> 00:51:29,030
I'm stressed here.

594
00:51:29,030 --> 00:51:30,100
Kidding.

595
00:52:30,070 --> 00:52:32,130
What are you doing sitting out here alone?

596
00:52:43,430 --> 00:52:45,070
Since you're here anyway,

597
00:52:52,170 --> 00:52:55,100
can I ask you straight?

598
00:52:59,400 --> 00:53:01,800
You like me, don't you?

599
00:53:05,030 --> 00:53:07,470
Not as a friend. More than that.

600
00:53:07,470 --> 00:53:08,570
Yes.

601
00:53:10,730 --> 00:53:12,130
Don't make that face.

602
00:53:12,900 --> 00:53:14,800
I'm the one who likes you.

603
00:53:15,270 --> 00:53:17,470
So it's on me to deal with my own feelings.

604
00:53:19,200 --> 00:53:20,930
But thank you, really.

605
00:53:21,600 --> 00:53:23,370
For being straight with me.

606
00:53:30,370 --> 00:53:34,670
So... I'm not going to lose a good friend like you, am I?

607
00:53:35,330 --> 00:53:37,100
If I...

608
00:54:09,430 --> 00:54:13,770
Honestly, I already knew the answer.

609
00:54:27,830 --> 00:54:29,670
It hurts.

610
00:54:38,230 --> 00:54:44,800
But I... I respect your decision, Fuen.

611
00:55:18,870 --> 00:55:21,770
"I know you're the most accurate fortune teller in the world."

612
00:55:21,770 --> 00:55:26,730
"If I want to ask about someone I secretly like, when's the best time to ask him?"

613
00:55:26,730 --> 00:55:33,230
"What an excellent question. Could you tell me what you're planning to ask about?"

614
00:55:37,930 --> 00:55:39,930
Help me out here, Chat.

615
00:55:39,930 --> 00:55:42,470
Praying to every holy thing out there.

616
00:55:46,370 --> 00:55:51,070
"I want to know what he really thinks of me."

617
00:55:53,130 --> 00:55:58,830
"Today, the best time to ask is... 17:29"

618
00:56:26,500 --> 00:56:29,670
Excuse me, have you seen Aof from M.6/1?

619
00:56:29,670 --> 00:56:31,200
Um, no, I haven't.

620
00:56:31,930 --> 00:56:36,170
Excuse me, have you seen Aof from M.6/1?

621
00:56:38,630 --> 00:56:39,870
Oh no.

622
00:56:52,400 --> 00:56:54,600
Aof. / Chemi.

623
00:56:59,700 --> 00:57:02,700
There's something I have to ask you.

624
00:57:02,700 --> 00:57:04,230
Calm down. Have some water first.

625
00:57:04,230 --> 00:57:05,430
It's all right.

626
00:57:06,500 --> 00:57:07,700
Aof.

627
00:57:07,700 --> 00:57:11,500
The promise you made me when I was a kid,

628
00:57:11,500 --> 00:57:13,630
do you still remember it?

629
00:57:25,000 --> 00:57:26,230
I...

630
00:57:26,230 --> 00:57:28,670
Just tell me yes or no. That's all.

631
00:57:45,970 --> 00:57:50,370
Hey, everyone, help! Star fell in the water!

632
00:58:10,930 --> 00:58:12,170
Come on, hurry.

633
00:58:12,170 --> 00:58:13,770
Holy shit.

634
00:58:13,770 --> 00:58:14,670
Hey, Star.

635
00:58:14,670 --> 00:58:16,200
Come on, quick.

636
00:58:16,200 --> 00:58:17,200
Holy shit.

637
00:58:17,200 --> 00:58:19,030
Are you okay? / Hey, help!

638
00:58:35,930 --> 00:58:37,330
Star.

639
00:59:27,300 --> 00:59:29,700
"Remember you said to tell you straight? I like Physics."

640
00:59:29,700 --> 00:59:32,300
"Easy to guess. The whole school knows you two like each other."

641
00:59:32,300 --> 00:59:34,900
"Since this is our last time talking, can we talk properly, Din?"

642
00:59:34,900 --> 00:59:38,670
"Honestly, I've felt awful. I only just realized how badly I treated you. Please forgive me."

643
00:59:39,030 --> 00:59:42,000
Physics has made it so damn obvious he's liked you since M.2.

644
00:59:42,000 --> 00:59:42,870
M.2?

645
00:59:42,870 --> 00:59:45,430
You idiot, you really had no idea?

646
00:59:46,030 --> 00:59:47,170
How did you stand it?

647
00:59:47,170 --> 00:59:48,330
Guess I like you too damn much.

648
00:59:48,330 --> 00:59:50,030
I never saw you as just a friend to begin with.

649
00:59:50,030 --> 00:59:50,900
I'm not ready.

650
00:59:50,900 --> 00:59:52,670
Whichever way you came, go back the same way.

651
00:59:52,670 --> 00:59:53,600
You may be my idol,

652
00:59:53,600 --> 00:59:55,070
but I have to protect my friend.

653
00:59:55,070 --> 00:59:56,530
I don't want Chemi misunderstanding me.

654
00:59:56,530 --> 00:59:59,500
It was Time shouting that let everyone know Star had fallen in.

655
00:59:59,500 --> 01:00:00,770
I'm hungry. Want to grab a bite?

656
01:00:00,770 --> 01:00:02,000
I talked to Fuen.

657
01:00:02,000 --> 01:00:03,200
At least I didn't lose a friend.

658
01:00:03,200 --> 01:00:07,230
But taking the person my friend likes? I just can't do it.

659
01:00:07,230 --> 01:00:08,800
Your heart is pounding right now.

660
01:00:08,800 --> 01:00:09,900
I like it.
